      "links": [
        { "label": "Source code", "url": "https://github.com/PhemeloMartin/Route-Runner" }
      ],
      "highlights": [
        { "title": "Learn, then do.", "text": "Every lesson leads into a quiz, a hands-on lab and a chapter boss, so each idea is practised straight after it is learned." },
        { "title": "Keeps it fresh.", "text": "Spaced-repetition flashcards, daily drills, CCNA-style mock exams, and a daily quest and streak that make revision a habit." },
        { "title": "Real commands.", "text": "In-browser simulators for Cisco IOS, an Ubuntu shell, docker, kubectl, terraform and dotnet respond like the real tools." },
        { "title": "Built like production.", "text": "A Fastify API with Zod validation, SQLite with tested migrations, Vitest suites, and Docker and Kubernetes manifests checked in CI." }
      ],
      "image": {
        "src": "/img/route-runner.jpg",
        "alt": "Route Runner: a 3D island seen from above, with a central plaza ringed by buildings labelled Cloud Tower, App Studio, Supercomputer, Server Room, Data Centre, PC Workshop and Exam Hall.",
        "width": 1440,
        "height": 810
      },
      "caseStudy": [
        {
          "heading": "Why I built it",
          "paragraphs": [
            "I wanted one place to learn and practise across the areas I work in, and a way to keep what I learn fresh instead of forgetting it after an exam.",
            "Route Runner turns that into a daily habit of about an hour: a daily quest always shows what to do next, a streak rewards showing up, and a 13-week study plan works towards the CCNA alongside cloud and DevOps."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "How it teaches",
          "bullets": [
            "Lessons in plain English, each with an analogy, key terms, \"say it like a pro\" lines to read aloud and an interview question to practise answering.",
            "A quiz after every lesson, then a hands-on lab, then a boss battle at the end of each chapter.",
            "Spaced-repetition flashcards (the SM-2 algorithm) and endless subnetting, binary, IPv6 and port drills to keep knowledge from fading.",
            "Mock exams weighted by the CCNA v2.0 blueprint, and XP, ranks and achievements that track progress in each area."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "What's inside",
          "bullets": [
            "Network Academy: 20 chapters and 59 lessons, from how a computer works to OSPF, ACLs, wireless and automation.",
            "Packet Lab: cable routers, switches and PCs on a 3D bench, then configure them with real Cisco IOS commands across 15 missions, including troubleshooting tickets.",
            "App Studio and Dev Studio: 13 chapters on C#, Dart, Git, Flutter, ASP.NET Core on .NET 10, EF Core, CI/CD and Kubernetes, with simulated dotnet, flutter, helm and GitHub Actions tools.",
            "Cloud Tower, Server Room and CloudShell: 12 chapters on Linux, virtualisation, AWS, Docker, Kubernetes and infrastructure as code, with an Ubuntu shell and a 3D cluster view where pods heal when a node fails.",
            "Data Centre, PC Workshop and Cable Bench: build a server rack, assemble a PC part by part, and crimp RJ45 cables to T568A and T568B."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "How the simulators work",
          "paragraphs": [ "The simulators are pure TypeScript and run in the browser, so labs respond instantly and work offline." ],
          "bullets": [
            "The network simulator models the decisions real devices make: interface status, VLANs and trunks, longest-prefix routing, OSPF with Dijkstra, DHCP, NAT, ACLs, HSRP and STP. A ping only succeeds if the reply can find its way back.",
            "The Cisco CLI is a table-driven parser with abbreviations, ? help and the same error messages as real IOS.",
            "The shell supports quotes, variables, pipes, redirection and scripts over a virtual filesystem with users and permissions, and the cloud tools share one machine, so curl can reach a container you just started."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Architecture and data",
          "bullets": [
            "A TypeScript monorepo with four packages: the simulation engine, the curriculum, a Fastify API and the React Three Fiber client.",
            "The curriculum is written as code in a small text format, and tests check that every lesson, question and lab link is complete.",
            "SQLite through WebAssembly, so nothing needs installing. XP is an append-only ledger, and a partial unique index stops a reward being claimed twice.",
            "Forward-only migrations, with a test that upgrades an old save and checks no progress is lost, plus atomic writes and daily backups."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Testing and delivery",
          "bullets": [
            "Vitest suites cover simulator scenarios such as OSPF convergence, DHCP relay, NAT and Kubernetes self-healing, plus API integration and curriculum integrity.",
            "GitHub Actions type-checks, tests and builds every push, smoke-tests the production server, validates the Kubernetes manifests and publishes a container image.",
            "A multi-stage, non-root Docker image with health checks, Kubernetes manifests with a network policy, and /healthz, /readyz and Prometheus /metrics endpoints."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
